Date: 2021-01-15

## Status

Proposed

## Context

In the migration from the v1 to the v2 of the ETL, the schema of the ingested data changed. The original schema is still relevant for backwards compatibility and the decision was made to still store it in the database and allow for 2 types of queries on that schema.

## Decision

To allow for two types of queries, one against the schema and one against the data, the decision was made to add a new method to the `Database` class called `UpdateRunningDatabase`. This method will take an `ILineRecord` as input and will allow for a single update on the `RunningDatabase` table. A new query will be built for each type of comparison and executed on the `RunningDatabase` table. This will allow a single line to be updated, deleted or inserted into the `RunningDatabase` table.

## Consequences

The implementation of this method will be relatively straightforward, however the code will have to branch on a few different values and will be an additional step for each change to the `Database` class. As a result a helper method, `UpdateRunningDatabaseCore` will be introduced, with `if/else` logic to build the query and call `ExecuteAsync` on the new query. Each method will accept a `ProjectionType` parameter, which will allow for branching on the type. This helper method will allow for the implementation of any future logic, such as a merge.

## Example Usage

```csharp
//Update the value of the current row
await _db.UpdateRunningDatabaseAsync(new IngestedDataRow() { Fields = new Dictionary<string, object>() { { "EventDate", DateTime.Parse("2020-01-10") } } });

//Update the row with a new value for Field1
await _db.UpdateRunningDatabaseAsync(new IngestedDataRow() { Fields = new Dictionary<string, object>() { { "Field1", 123 } } });

//Add a new row
await _db.AddRunningDatabaseAsync(new IngestedDataRow() { Fields = new Dictionary<string, object>() { { "Field1", 456 }, { "Field2", DateTime.Parse("2021-01-01") } } });
```

